audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Reading the news in Russian: a headline':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||The first snow, the bridges, a new metro station: read a short Petersburg news item and learn how a Russian headline is built.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:mb6tuh'
    '|a||Ноя́брь, у́тро. Я за́втракаю, and the radio reads the city news. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Здра́вствуйте! Но́вости Петербу́рга.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3240
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:159k2z'
    '|b||Сего́дня но́чью в го́роде вы́пал пе́рвый снег.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||Несмотря́ на снег, мосты́ бу́дут разводи́ть ещё две неде́ли.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4080
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||А на Васи́льевском о́строве откро́ется но́вая ста́нция метро́ — в декабре́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||What happened in the night?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1920
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||Вы́пал пе́рвый снег: the first snow fell.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3840
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||What about the bridges?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1880
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||Ещё две неде́ли: two more weeks.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3280
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||When does the new metro station open?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|b||В декабре́: in December.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2520
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Пото́м я чита́ю но́вости в телефо́не. Но́вости: the plural of но́вость.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В Петербу́рге вы́пал пе́рвый снег.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fhaxy6'
    '|b||A headline puts the verb before its subject, in the perfective past: it has happened. Вы́пал: fell.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1o5zkrm'
    '|a||На Васи́льевском — но́вая ста́нция.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:12okts9'
    '|b||No verb at all: the dash says is, or will be.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4080
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1v5l1hk'
    '|a||За́втра — ми́нус пять. Short lines, few words.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1yswh5j'
    '|a||Пого́да: ми́нус оди́н. Жи́тели ра́ды.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:13iho32'
    '|b||Произошло́ собы́тие: большо́е собы́тие.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3360
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:h0cjnb'
    '|a||Постро́или ста́нцию: совреме́нную ста́нцию.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:p47aek'
    '|b||Одна́ко: however. You''ll read it far more often than you hear it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:ausm19'
    '|b||Прочита́йте. The whole item, on three pages, with the new words glossed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1i2balj'
    '|a||В Петербу́рге вы́пал пе́рвый снег':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1pnxkm5'
    '|a||Сего́дня но́чью в го́роде произошло́ большо́е собы́тие: вы́пал пе́рвый снег.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:8xakxg'
    '|a||Пого́да днём — ми́нус оди́н гра́дус и ве́тер.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1gjyxpa'
    '|b||Произошло́ ends in о, because собы́тие is an it-word.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:wai62b'
    '|b||The verb comes before its subject, so look after it for the subject.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4480
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:ks4azv'
    '|b||Да́льше: the roads, and the bridges.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3400
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1syov12'
    '|a||Жи́тели ра́ды: у́тром го́род стал бе́лым.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1dolcsu'
    '|a||Одна́ко на доро́гах бы́ло мно́го маши́н, и лю́ди опа́здывали на рабо́ту.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:gfqw9f'
    '|a||Несмотря́ на снег, мосты́ бу́дут разводи́ть ещё две неде́ли.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:v69k80'
    '|a||Одна́ко turns the good news round: however, the roads were full.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1n9mpef'
    '|b||Да́льше: and the island''s news.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:19s6pr6'
    '|a||А на Васи́льевском о́строве постро́или совреме́нную ста́нцию метро́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:15h83qu'
    '|a||Её вы́ход — пря́мо на на́бережную.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:aapzef'
    '|a||Ста́нция откро́ется в декабре́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:y9t6jh'
    '|b||Постро́или has no subject: they built. Who doesn''t matter, as in мне предложи́ли рабо́ту.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:wh1ecr'
    '|b||Запо́лните про́пуски: three verbs. Look after each verb for its subject.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:fomxqy'
    '|b||Запо́лните про́пуски.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1760
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:175nu37'
    '|a||Но́чью вы́пал снег.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2040
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В го́роде произошло́ собы́тие.':
      mp3: 
